        "original_id": "afa0a609-70c3-53bd-980b-288b0a58296a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John O'Hara, Rabindranath Tagore\n- Works: Elizabeth Appleton\n- Topics: American writing, Bengali literature and music, Indian art, social realism, Contextual Modernism\n\nFacts:\n- Rabindranath Tagore, also written Ravīndranātha Thākura and known by the sobriquet Gurudev, lived from 7 May 1861 to 7 August 1941.\n- Rabindranath Tagore was a Bengali polymath who reshaped Bengali literature and music and influenced Indian art through Contextual Modernism in the late 19th and early 20th centuries.\n- John Henry O'Hara lived from January 31, 1905 to April 11, 1970.\n- John O'Hara was an American writer best remembered for observing social status and manners in early to mid-20th-century America and for depicting social realism.\n- Elizabeth Appleton is a novel by John O'Hara that was first published in 1963.",
